Subject: [PATCH 06946/11362] [outer-loop] Task 7: /think vs /no_think
 induction quality A/B (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5594)

Fixed a false-negative bug in the think-mode/MTP compatibility precondition
check before the real A/B could run: the first probe reported incompatible
because its tag detector ("<think>" in content) missed the "<thinking>" tag
variant the model actually emitted, and its 1.5x length-ratio fallback was
too strict for a short n_predict=120 probe (549 vs 403 chars, a real 36%
delta, rejected). Fixed by matching a tuple of known reasoning-tag prefixes
and lowering the length fallback to 1.15x; re-verified against two
independent manual probes.

Also discovered, independent of the A/B result: LocalGGUFProposer's
no_think_prefix attribute has no effect on real induction calls today --
CARNOT_ARC_CODEONLY_INDUCE (default ON) hardcodes its own /no_think via
_L2_CODEONLY_DIRECTIVE, which wins over the instance attribute. Testing
/think required a scoped monkeypatch of that constant instead.

Real 4-attempt measurement (m0r0 + sk48, both arms, live Qwen3.5-9B-MTP,
161.6s): both arms induced successfully on both games; heldout_accuracy --
m0r0 no_think=0.5 vs think=0.0, sk48 tied at 1.0. honest_verdict:
think_mode_ab_equal_success_no_think_higher_accuracy. Neither game's
window contained a real level-up, so goal-predicate accuracy (REQ-ARC-
WMTE-5593) is unmeasured -- disclosed, not papered over. Per the frozen-
live-stack guardrail, the /no_think live config is unchanged; this result
gives no evidence to justify unfreezing it.

